# SRG-APP-000115-AU-000160  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to perform on-demand filtering
# of the log records for events of interest based on organization-defined
# criteria.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000115-AU-000160
group:           V-206456
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000158
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    The Splunk search language performs on-demand filtering over the indexed
                 records, and role configuration determines which indexes a filtering user
                 may search.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.

check:           authorize.conf [] srchIndexesAllowed non_empty

external:        The criteria themselves - which events are of interest - are
                 organization-defined and held in the site security plan, so the criterion
                 tests only that the product can filter the records on demand.
external:        On-demand filtering is performed by the search language, which is
                 intrinsic to the product and has no configuration surface to assert.

citation:        OVER-REACH, and two conditions nothing can satisfy. The original ANDed
                 four independent features - event types, macros, saved searches and role
                 index access - so an instance expressing its criteria through any one of
                 them fails for lacking the other three. Two could never pass on a stock
                 instance: the shipped eventtypes.conf and savedsearches.conf both declare
                 "search =" empty in their default stanzas, and macros.conf is not shipped
                 at all, so definition non_empty reads nothing. Where a site has expressed
                 its criteria as event types, macros or saved searches, those are read as
                 evidence of the organization-defined criteria rather than demanded as a
                 conjunction.
finding:         No role is permitted to search the indexes holding the records
                 (srchIndexesAllowed is unset), so on-demand filtering for events of
                 interest cannot be performed against them.
